# Live credentials. Never commit.
#
# This repo has a GitHub remote. The existing pm-backend-php repo has
# live database credentials sitting in a public repository — that is the
# exact mistake this line exists to prevent on the product whose whole
# pitch is that data does not leak.
#
# Verify before every push:  git ls-files api/config.php   (must be empty)
api/config.php

# NOTE: api/setup.php is deliberately NOT ignored, so it deploys with the
# code on a fresh install. It refuses to run once an administrator
# exists, but "refuses to run" is not "is not there" — delete it from the
# server the moment the first admin is created.

# Certificate material. The CA signing key is the root of the entire
# device-authentication layer; if it leaks, anyone can mint a laptop
# certificate and the whole mTLS story is over.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.crl

# Local
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
*.bak
*.swp

# Standalone connection diagnostic. Prints database name, user and host.
# Delete from the server after use.
api/dbtest.php
